# No delegating method aliases

Do not add a method whose entire body only calls another method on the **same** receiver (or only returns `t.field`) when the two names mean the same thing to callers. Pick one entry point and put the logic there.

## Do not

```go
// BAD — Process is a useless alias for fanOut
func (e *Engine) Process(ctx context.Context, env *core.Envelope) {
	e.fanOut(ctx, *env)
}

// BAD — re-export wrappers on the same type when embedding works
func (b *SharedBuffer) TryEnqueue(env *core.Envelope) bool {
	return b.buf.TryEnqueue(env)
}
```

Prefer **embedding** or **call the real method** from outside the type.

## Allowed

- **Shared implementation, multiple entry points:** `Init(ctx) { return s.Reload(ctx) }` when `Reload` is also invoked from SIGHUP or other paths.
- **Interface requirements:** `slog.Handler` decorators that forward `Enabled` / `WithAttrs` / `WithGroup` to an inner handler.
- **Field accessors** that expose an injected or constructed dependency (`TracerProvider() trace.TracerProvider { return p.providers.TracerProvider }`).
- **Small package-level functions** that are not duplicate names on the same type (e.g. `Provide() pal.ServiceDef` in `services.go`).

When refactoring, merge the wrapper into the kept name or use embedding instead of forward-only methods.
